    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm taking the Eurostar from St Pancras to Paris next week. What are the current rules for heavy luggage? I'm worried about the weight limits and how much time I need to leave for checking in bags.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar is a very sturdy train, but you should be aware that the luggage policy is quite strict, and the staff are very vigilant about it. Heavy luggage is generally limited to two large suitcases and one small bag, and the total weight must not exceed 125kg (275lbs) for the entire journey. If you exceed this weight limit, you will be charged a significant fee, which is much more expensive than the standard ticket price.\n\nRegarding the timing, you need to arrive at St Pancras at least 45 minutes before departure to check in your bags. This is because the baggage handling process is quite time-consuming, and the staff are very busy. If you arrive late, you might miss your train, and the train crew will not let you board with heavy luggage if you are not ready. It is also worth noting that the train crew is very strict about the rules, and they will not allow you to board with heavy luggage if you are not ready.\n\nTo avoid any issues, you should check the Eurostar website for the latest information, as the rules can change. It is always better to be safe than sorry, and to avoid any potential fines or delays.",
